  "implemented": [
    "Public ordinary, template and member enable-if overloads bind canonical Sema expression profiles with lexical parameter slots, types and resolved declaration identities instead of AST pointers.",
    "Ordered condition sequences and multiplicity preserve native prefix priority; predicates with different owners/operators/parentheses remain distinct. Moving sources and renaming parameters preserve native USRs.",
    "AST import compares canonical predicate shapes and their corresponding typed bindings, including reference declaration scopes. Template and ordinary overloads remain separate.",
    "Publication binds ordered conditions and diagnostic messages through the existing native declaration-attribute capability; private predicate dependencies are rejected.",
    "Polished printing preserves free/member declaration grammar, parameter scope around assembly labels, and inherited diagnostic predicates in definitions with unnamed parameters and authored body locals.",
    "Source-free provider calls exercise ordinary/template/member selection, ordered priority, named/unnamed predicate bindings and rejection of disabled calls/address-taking. C17 single-entry predicates replay."
  ],
  "scope": [
    "Runtime sources, service binaries and GNUstep binaries are unchanged. No SDK archive or complete five-family runtime source/PCH matrix was rebuilt/rerun; that matrix remains recorded at source 2.91.",
    "Final native/frontend/package reports bind their compiler, checker and fixture inputs. Focused source-free packages cover C++20/C++23, ARC/MRC, O0/O2 and normal/eager/ASan+UBSan/TSan after provider source removal and package relocation. The full fixture has three smoke configurations.",
    "Parentheses distinguish native enable-if overloads; an initial test incorrectly assumed otherwise. The corrected native witness checks that distinction. Earlier failed reports remain separate.",
    "C overloadable package publication, further predicate/declaration forms, general standard-library publication, remaining ownership/concurrency/isolation/key-path/language/profile work and native Linux AArch64 remain open."
  ],
